33,2,,status,George,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The row under the eaves is dry, but the rest get rained on. Four times a day, someone shifts a bike.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The ledger shows no capital work. The ward park costs 2,600 yen monthly, with fourteen households waiting.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,The minutes show the same flats held the covered spots for five years. The sticker register shows daily riders want to pay.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The complaint log has nine notes about leaning bikes, all ignored. The neighbouring block had three households in arrears.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Mio,,The treasurer spends three hours a month reconciling cash. The display frame takes twenty seconds to load and needs greasing.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, 2,600 yen is high, but the rain here is worse. I need a solution that stops the shifting.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, the ward park is expensive. But if we charge internally, we cover the cost. I need to see the numbers.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Shunichi, arrears are bad. But the minutes prove the bias. We need a fairer system, not just a cheaper one.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@George, bias is one thing. Arrears are another. I don't want to chase money. I want peace.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Ryuji, three hours a month is a lot. If we add billing, that doubles. I need to know if we can handle it.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"The shifting is the real problem. If we have fixed spots, the morning rush stops.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"Fixed spots mean fixed costs. If we charge, we cover the maintenance. I support a paid model.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"Fixed spots are what we have now, and they are unfair. A lottery might be better, but it feels random.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"A lottery is random, but it is fair. It avoids the resentment of ""who gets the good spot.""","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Mio,,A lottery is simple. But who manages it? I don't want to be the one chasing people for fees.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"I prefer fixed spots, but they must be assigned fairly. I am leaning towards a lottery.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I prefer paid allocation. It covers the costs and gives people a stake. I am leaning towards paid.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,"I am torn. The lottery is fair, but the paid model is practical. I need to think.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,I am leaning towards the lottery. It is the least likely to cause social friction.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Mio,,I am leaning towards the lottery. It is the simplest to manage. I don't want the billing headache.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
